<p><strong>Gym membership software for Nepal should track prepaid membership tiers and renewals, let members book classes and trainer sessions, count down session packages, control discounts, and show the owner one report across branches. Zennly covers these for gyms, fitness studios and personal trainers.</strong></p>
<p>Gym software is one of the most crowded categories in Nepal, with many local products. Most are strong at member lists and fee reminders. The gaps appear when a gym adds classes, personal training, several branches, or staff who give discounts. That is where the choice matters.</p>
<h2>Start with your real problems</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Fees and renewals.</strong> Who has paid, until when, and who has lapsed? See <a href="/features/memberships/">memberships</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Classes and trainers.</strong> A class or trainer slot should be bookable and should not be double-booked. See <a href="/features/booking/">booking management</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Session packages.</strong> Ten personal-training sessions are a package with a count. See <a href="/features/packages/">packages</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Discounts.</strong> Joining offers and festival discounts leak money when nobody approves them. Read <a href="/blog/discount-leakage/">discount leakage</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Trainer pay.</strong> Salary plus commission is easier with <a href="/features/payroll/">payroll</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Questions to ask every vendor</h2>
<ul>
<li>Can members book classes and trainers online?</li>
<li>How are renewals, expiry and top-ups recorded?</li>
<li>Who approves a discount, and is it recorded?</li>
<li>Can I see every branch in one report?</li>
<li>Which payment methods do I need, and does the vendor support them? Ask this in every demo and get the answer in writing.</li>
<li>How is it priced? See <a href="/blog/booking-software-price-nepal/">what affects the price</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Compared with other gym tools</h2>
<p>We keep a plain comparison of what to ask every vendor on <a href="/compare/gym-software-nepal/">gym software in Nepal, compared</a>. Use it with any product you are evaluating.</p>
<h2>See it for your gym</h2>
<p>Read how <a href="/solutions/fitness/">gyms and fitness studios</a> use Zennly, or the earlier guide to <a href="/blog/gym-management-nepal/">gym management in Nepal</a>.</p>

<h2>Signs your gym has outgrown a notebook</h2>
<ul>
<li>Nobody can say, in under a minute, how many members are active today.</li>
<li>Renewals are chased from memory, and some lapse unnoticed.</li>
<li>Trainers and classes clash because nothing locks a slot.</li>
<li>Discounts at joining time are agreed verbally and never recorded.</li>
<li>A second branch opens and the owner no longer sees one clear picture.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How to move over without a disruption</h2>
<ol>
<li>Start with new members and new bookings in the system, and let existing records stay where they are.</li>
<li>Enter your membership tiers, class types and trainers.</li>
<li>Run in parallel for a week: check the system against the notebook every evening.</li>
<li>Retire the notebook once the numbers match.</li>
</ol>
<p>Ask every vendor to show this migration on your own data in the demo.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>What is the best gym management software in Nepal?</h3>
      <p>It depends on your gym. For member records and fee reminders only, a simple gym tool may do. For gyms that run classes, trainers, session packages and several branches and want discount control, Zennly is built for that.</p>
      <h3>Can Zennly manage gym membership fees and renewals?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Zennly tracks membership tiers with a wallet balance, validity period, top-ups and renewals.</p>
      <h3>Can members book classes and trainers online?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Classes and trainer sessions can be scheduled and booked online with payments recorded per booking.</p>
      <h3>Can I run more than one gym branch?</h3>
      <p>Yes, from one account with one daily report across all branches.</p>
      
